{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegralRecursionLattice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegralRecursionLattice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.lattice_span_fg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.lattice_span_fg","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L368-L385","doc":"**The whole `ℓ ≥ 0` lattice is finitely generated.**  Composing\n`lattice_in_row_zero_span` (the 2-D → 1-D collapse) with `row_zero_span_fg`,\nthe submodule spanned by every `I_{m,ℓ}` with `ℓ ≥ 0` coincides with the\nrow-0 submodule and is therefore `Submodule.FG` (by `≤ max{A,B}`\ngenerators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_span_fg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_span_fg","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L360-L366","doc":"**Row 0 is finitely generated.**  The submodule spanned by the entire\ntwo-sided row `ℓ = 0` is `Submodule.FG` (by `≤ max{A,B}` generators, via\n`row_zero_fg_bound`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_fg_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_fg_bound","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L330-L358","doc":"**Finite generation with an explicit `≤ max{A,B}` bound.**  The row-0\nsubmodule `span R {I_{j,0} : j ∈ ℤ}` is generated by the explicit finite set\n`{I_{0,0}, …, I_{max{A,B}−1,0}}` — a `Finset` of cardinality `≤ max{A,B}`.\n\nThis is the literal \"`max{A,B}` independent integrals\" bound of FW: `≥`\nis `row_zero_in_window` (every generator reduces into the window), `≤` is\nthat each window element is itself a row-0 integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_in_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_in_window","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L265-L328","doc":"**Two-sided ℤ reduction of row 0 into a fixed size-`max{A,B}` window.**\nEvery row-0 integral `I_{m,0}`, for *any* `m ∈ ℤ`, lies in the `R`-span of\nthe single fundamental window `{I_{0,0}, I_{1,0}, …, I_{max{A,B}−1,0}}`.\n\nThis is the full finite-generation core FW's \"`max{A,B}` independent\nintegrals\" corollary rests on: the entire two-sided row `ℓ = 0` reduces into\none size-`max{A,B}` window.  The proof is two `ℕ`-indexed strong inductions:\n\n* **upward** (`hUp`, `∀ n : ℕ, I_{n,0} ∈ W`): indices `< max{A,B}` are window\n  generators; an index `n ≥ max{A,B}` is pushed *down* by\n  `row_zero_top_reduction` (base `n − max{A,B}`) into `{I_{n−max,0}, …,\n  I_{n−1,0}}`, every element of which is a strictly-smaller natural index —\n  strong IH.\n* **downward** (`hDown`, `∀ n : ℕ, I_{−n−1,0} ∈ W`): `row_zero_bot_reduction`\n  pushes `I_{−n−1,0}` *up* into `{I_{−n,0}, …, I_{−n−1+max,0}}`; each element\n  is either a nonnegative index (covered by `hUp`) or a strictly-smaller\n  negative index — strong IH. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_bot_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_bot_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L225-L263","doc":"**Bottom-of-window reduction (m-direction one step, mirror image).**  The\nbottom index of the order-`max{A,B}` recurrence, `I_{m,0}`, lies in the span\nof the window *above* it, `{I_{m+1,0}, …, I_{m+max{A,B},0}}`.\n\nThis is the mirror of `row_zero_top_reduction`: it shifts any row-0 index\n*up* toward a size-`max{A,B}` fundamental domain.  Unlike the top reduction,\nno case split on `A ≠ B` is needed — the `k = 0` term of\n`row_zero_recurrence` always carries the unit coefficient\n`C(B,0)·(−1)^0 = 1`, so `I_{m,0}` is isolated directly:\n\n  `I_{m,0} = (−1)^A q^{A+m}·I_{m+A,0} − ∑_{k=1}^{B} C(B,k)(−1)^k I_{m+k,0}`,\n\nand every index on the right (`m+A` with `1 ≤ A ≤ max{A,B}`, and `m+k` with\n`1 ≤ k ≤ B ≤ max{A,B}`) lies in the up-window.  (No `hq` hypothesis: the\nisolated coefficient is `1`, so no inverse is taken.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_top_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_top_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L176-L223","doc":"**Top-of-window reduction (m-direction one step).**  The top index of\nthe order-`max{A,B}` recurrence, `I_{m+max{A,B},0}`, lies in the span\nof the fundamental window `{I_{m,0}, …, I_{m+max{A,B}−1,0}}`.\n\nThis is the single-step reduction that shifts any row-0 index toward a\nsize-`max{A,B}` fundamental domain — the algebraic core of FW's\n\"`max{A,B}` independent integrals\".  Two cases on `A ≠ B`:\nif `B < A` the top is the `A`-shift (`row_zero_solve_A` + span\nmonotonicity); if `A < B` the top is the `B`-term, isolated from the\nrecurrence (its coefficient `(−1)^B` is a unit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_solve_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_solve_A","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L154-L174","doc":"**A-shift reduction.** The `A`-shifted row-0 integral `I_{m+A,0}` is an\n`R`-linear combination of the `B`-window `{I_{m,0}, …, I_{m+B,0}}`.\nSolve `row_zero_recurrence` for `I_{m+A,0}` (its coefficient\n`(−1)^A q^{A+m}` is a unit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.lattice_in_row_zero_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.lattice_in_row_zero_span","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L145-L152","doc":"**2-D → 1-D collapse.** The entire `ℓ ≥ 0` half-lattice lies in the\n`R`-span of the row `ℓ = 0`.  Immediate from `ell_collapse`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.ell_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.ell_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L121-L143","doc":"**ℓ-collapse.** For every `n : ℕ` and `m : ℤ`, the integral `I_{m,n}`\nis a *nonzero* scalar multiple of a single row-0 integral:\n\n  `I_{m,n} = c · I_{m + n·A, 0}`,  `c ≠ 0`.\n\nThe ℓ-direction of the lattice is fully determined by row `ℓ = 0`.\nProof: iterate `relation_r`; the coefficient is a product of the\nunits `(−1)^A` and `q^{A+·}` (nonzero since `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.row_zero_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L105-L119","doc":"The order-`max{A,B}` linear recurrence on the row `ℓ = 0`, obtained\nby equating the two sides of (FW 14) at `ℓ = 0` (where `q^{−0·k} = 1`):\n\n  `(−1)^A q^{A+m} · I_{m+A,0} = ∑_{k=0}^{B} C(B,k)(−1)^k I_{m+k,0}`.\n\nThis relates the `max{A,B}+1` consecutive row-0 integrals\n`I_{m,0}, …, I_{m+max{A,B},0}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.relation_r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.relation_r","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Right equality of (FW 14): the single-shift relation.\n`I_{m,ℓ+1} = (−1)^A q^{A+m} I_{m+A,ℓ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.relation_l","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.relation_l","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Left equality of (FW 14): the raising-in-ℓ relation.\n`I_{m,ℓ+1} = ∑_{k=0}^{B} C(B,k)(−1)^k q^{−ℓk} I_{m+k,ℓ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.hAB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.hAB","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L93-L93","doc":"FW setup: `A ≠ B` (so `max{A,B}` is a strict maximum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.hB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.hB","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L91-L91","doc":"FW setup: `B` is a positive integer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.hA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.hA","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L89-L89","doc":"FW setup: `A` is a positive integer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StateIntegral.Recursion","kind":"class","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StateIntegralRecursionLattice.lean#L75-L103","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** carrying Fantini–Wheeler eq. (14).\n\n`Recursion R M A B q I` asserts that the family\n`I : ℤ → ℤ → M`, `I m ℓ = I_{m,ℓ}`, satisfies the two FW relations\nfor the positive integers `A ≠ B` and the deformation parameter `q`.\nEach field is the recursion itself (a parameter-quantified equation\nin `M`), NOT a conclusion — this is the FW INPUT, to be *assumed*;\nthe theorems below DERIVE the algebraic lattice structure from it.\n\nThis is the analytic content FW prove for the actual integrals; here\nit is axiomatized so the downstream algebra can be checked by Lean. ","signatureChunk":0}]}